#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186221141 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f2e37d37-007c-569b-a44c-cb6a9d075371" :knowledge-point/title "Differentiating a Fourier Series"}] :question/id #uuid "669126b0-2995-549c-9a80-888bccd3acc5" :question/math-academy-id "e-21845" :question/problem "Let $f(x)$ be the $10$-periodic extension of the function\n$F(x)=\\dfrac{5}{2}x^2-3$\ndefined on $[-5,5).$ Fill in the blanks in the reasoning below, showing the derivation of the Fourier series of the $10$-periodic extension of $G(x)=5x$\nfrom the corresponding Fourier series of $f(x).$\n\nThe Fourier series of $f(x)$ is given by\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14069003/assets/178be718fdba262f895193f9c503667f4ba3f709db23717893016d500ba4bc8b.png)\nSince $f$ is ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14069003/assets/6c274adc750119956ce950c5212283e01dfddf37137178bf0b85295a6837f433.png)\nand  ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14069003/assets/6c274adc750119956ce950c5212283e01dfddf37137178bf0b85295a6837f433.png)\non $\\mathbb{R},$ we may differentiate its Fourier series term-by-term to get\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14069003/assets/9d14fd1a227fc073b09d78684cb8dbff507bf083da988dda2755270a77981455.png)" :question/worked-solution "First, notice that $F(x)$ is an even function. So, the Fourier series of its $2L$-periodic extension has the form\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{a_0}{2} + \\sum_{n=1}^\\infty a_n \\cos\\left(\\dfrac{n\\pi x}{L}\\right).\n$$\n\nIn our case, $L=5.$ Thus, the Fourier series of $f(x)$ is given by\n\n$$\nf(x) \\sim \\dfrac{107}{6}\n+ \\sum_{n=1}^\\infty \\dfrac{250(-1)^n}{n^2\\pi^2}\n\\bbox[4pt, border: solid 0.5pt black]{\\cos\\left(\\dfrac{n\\pi x}{5}\\right)}.\n$$\n\nNow, notice that  \n\n- the function $F$ is continuously differentiable on $(-5,5),$\n\n- continuous on $[-5,5),$ and\n\n- satisfies $F(-5)=F(5),$ if we extend the value at $x=5$ using the formula $F(x)=\\dfrac{5}{2}x^2-3.$\n\nTherefore, the $10$-periodic extension $f$ is $\\bbox[4pt, border: solid 0.5pt black]{\\text{continuous} }$ and $\\bbox[4pt, border: solid 0.5pt black]{\\text{piecewise smooth}}$\non $\\mathbb{R},$ so we may differentiate its Fourier series term-by-term:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{5}{2}{x}^{2}-3) & ∼\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{107}{6})+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{250(-1)^{n}}{{n}^{2}{\\pi }^{2}}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{5})) \\\\ 5x & ∼0+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{250(-1)^{n}}{{n}^{2}{\\pi }^{2}}\\cdot (-\\frac{n\\pi }{5}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{5})) \\\\ 5x & ∼{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{-50(-1)^{n}}{n\\pi }\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{5}) \\\\ 5x & ∼{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{50(-1)^{n+1}}{n\\pi }\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{5}).\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186221142 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "2ae32a2a-438f-547c-8510-7e9f760c3cb6" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Properties of Periodic Extensions"}] :question/id #uuid "6e45e60d-7c68-5c49-8ca2-5381af39cd47" :question/math-academy-id "e-21846" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14069003/assets/9b34c017e88b9ed4f80f45223c5093a2f934d249d666b3c1d929718bc05e9882.png)\nThe above function $F(x)$ is defined on $x \\in [-2,2).$ Let $f(x)$ be the $4$-periodic extension of $F(x)$ to $x\\in\\mathbb{R}.$\nDetermine whether each statement below is true or false.\n\n- $F(x)$ is continuous on $x\\in(-2,2).$\n\n- $F(x)$ is piecewise smooth on $x\\in(-2,2).$\n\n- $\\lim\\limits_{x \\to -2^+} F(x) = \\lim\\limits_{x \\to 2^-} F(x).$\n\n- $f(x)$ is piecewise smooth and continuous on $\\mathbb{R}.$" :question/worked-solution "Let's examine the given statements in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true. The function $F(x)$ is continuous on $x \\in (-2,2).$ Its graph is shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14069003/assets/5c1cc57825a318df088ac0bc28ffe75c21579c5fe007fbb52cf0710a1937dc1e.png)\n\n- Statement II is true. The function $F(x)$ is piecewise smooth on $x \\in (-2,2).$ It consists of two smooth pieces.\n\n- Statement III is true. Indeed, we have\n\n$$\n\\lim\\limits_{x \\to -2^+} F(x) = \\lim\\limits_{x \\to -2^+} (-2x) = -2(-2) = 4\n$$\n\nand \n\n$$\n\\lim\\limits_{x \\to 2^-} F(x) = \\lim\\limits_{x \\to 2^-} x^2 = (2)^2 = 4.\n$$\n\nSo, $\\lim\\limits_{x \\to -2^+} F(x) = \\lim\\limits_{x \\to 2^-} F(x).$\n\n- Statement IV is true since statements I, II, and III are all true.\n\n**Note:** The $4$-periodic extension of $F(x)$ to $x \\in \\mathbb{R}$ has the graph shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14069003/assets/f5fb59869184a0c54ddaeea0b434104f3335c652c3f7533cd9dec0dcdcc91876.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186221143 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c1e01d04-6c13-52eb-a4b6-ad9a5cde8134" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating a Fourier Series"}] :question/id #uuid "77c71e9d-c2a4-5a2c-9c67-a90e8913ba13" :question/math-academy-id "e-21856" :question/problem "Let $f(x)$ be the $8$-periodic extension of the function $F(x)=-\\dfrac{3}{4}x^2$ defined on $[-4,4).$ Fill in the blanks in the reasoning below, showing the derivation of a series converging to the $8$-periodic extension of \n\n$$\nG(x) = -\\dfrac{1}{4}x^3 = \\int_0^x f(t) \\, \\text{d}t\n$$\n\nfrom the corresponding Fourier series of $f(x).$\n\nThe Fourier series of $f(x)$ is given by\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14069003/assets/7ddcc5e5d8580428341aec84ff2982c593054ec7ec363cc11139d87912dab58d.png)\n Since $f$ is \n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14069003/assets/91f9e216819e2259c6cc4ce19c39e38f8d75c9a5902019de9e437e0732477943.png)\non $\\mathbb{R},$ we may integrate its Fourier series term-by-term to get\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14069003/assets/1c6cf5957b07d2564607d603276b7fb9cffbe7502f53c6ea77a10b726d95aefd.png)" :question/worked-solution "First, notice that $F(x)$ is an even function. So, the Fourier series of its $2L$-periodic extension has the form\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{a_0}{2}+\\sum_{n=1}^\\infty a_n \\cos\\left(\\dfrac{n\\pi x}{L}\\right).\n$$\n\nIn our case, $L=4$ and we are already given the coefficients for $n \\geq 1.$ Thus, the Fourier series of $f(x)$ is given by\n\n$$\nf(x) \\sim -4+\\sum_{n=1}^\\infty \\dfrac{48(-1)^{n+1}}{n^2\\pi^2}\n\\bbox[4pt, border: solid 0.5pt black]{\\cos\\left(\\dfrac{n\\pi x}{4}\\right)}.\n$$\n\nNow, notice that the function $F$ is continuous on $(-4,4).$ \nTherefore, the $8$-periodic extension $f$ is $\\bbox[4pt, border: solid 0.5pt black]{\\text{piecewise continuous}}$ on $\\mathbb{R},$ so we may integrate its Fourier series term-by-term:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{x}(-\\frac{3}{4}{t}^{2})\\,\\text{d}t & ∼{\\int }_{0}^{x}(-4+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{48(-1)^{n+1}}{{n}^{2}{\\pi }^{2}}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi t}{4}))\\text{d}t \\\\ {[-\\frac{1}{4}{t}^{3}]}_{0}^{x} & ∼{[-4t]}_{0}^{x}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{48(-1)^{n+1}}{{n}^{2}{\\pi }^{2}}\\cdot [\\frac{4}{n\\pi }\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi t}{4})]_{0}^{x} \\\\ -\\frac{1}{4}{x}^{3} & ∼-4x+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\,\\frac{192(-1)^{n+1}}{{n}^{3}{\\pi }^{3}}\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{4})\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186221961 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "2ae32a2a-438f-547c-8510-7e9f760c3cb6" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Properties of Periodic Extensions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9028c9b4-0eb1-5e1d-8cbb-b8155bf83fdb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "False" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186220739} {:answer/id #uuid "42d01fd9-eb03-57e5-bc69-1b1db7f60d62" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "True" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186220740}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "42d01fd9-eb03-57e5-bc69-1b1db7f60d62" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "True" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186220740} :answer-field/id #uuid "d7a167be-384f-5c25-9282-cb9ba2153373" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186220738} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9b543458-7e54-561a-9075-86139e3b8880" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "True" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186220742} {:answer/id #uuid "d50e4592-528d-5165-9cb2-a253443b9bed" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "False" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186220743}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9b543458-7e54-561a-9075-86139e3b8880" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "True" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186220742} :answer-field/id #uuid "5cc5726b-446b-5ee4-a6c8-b77ca10a46f0" :answer-field/key "field-4" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186220741} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e0adb0fd-986e-5eb1-b42e-e5710d8afacf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "True" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186220745} {:answer/id #uuid "3c8a4d8e-07d8-50dd-a0c9-57ba54723b07" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "False" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186220746}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e0adb0fd-986e-5eb1-b42e-e5710d8afacf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "True" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186220745} :answer-field/id #uuid "a10dc220-6ce1-5d98-a8a8-fb09c06c9618" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186220744} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f03ee50b-c228-57c5-a275-7737e1307621" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "False" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186220748} {:answer/id #uuid "1b1352ba-0c32-552c-a5e2-a62209416db8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "True" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186220749}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1b1352ba-0c32-552c-a5e2-a62209416db8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "True" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186220749} :answer-field/id #uuid "04c0ac69-b2e7-5d82-8067-b78da40a0950" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186220747}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "2cc2bb4c-12ce-5499-9381-7f752bdaab23" :question/math-academy-id "q-341129" :question/problem "$$\nF(x)={\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}, & x\\in [0,3) \\\\ -3x, & x\\in [-3,0)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe above function $F(x)$ is defined on $x\\in [-3,3).$ Let $f(x)$ be the $6$-periodic extension of $F(x)$ to $x\\in R.$\nSelect the correct options below.\n\n| I. | $F(x)$ is continuous on $x\\in (-3,3)$ | {{field-1}} |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| II. | $F(x)$ is piecewise smooth on $x\\in (-3,3)$ | {{field-2}} |\n| III. | ${lim}_{x\\to -{3}^{+}}F(x)={lim}_{x\\to {3}^{-}}F(x)$ | {{field-3}} |\n| IV. | $f(x)$ is piecewise smooth and continuous on $R$ | {{field-4}} |" :question/worked-solution "Let's examine the given statements in turn.\n\n- Statement I is $\\text{true}.$ The function $F(x)$ is continuous on $x\\in (-3,3).$ Its graph is shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14069003/assets/186106373f9848cfefefb23197e7508497ff3d570f326da2ca342d078682128d.png)\n\n- Statement II is $\\text{true}.$ The function $F(x)$ is piecewise smooth on $x\\in (-3,3).$ It consists of two smooth pieces.\n\n- Statement III is $\\text{true}.$ Indeed, we have\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to -{3}^{+}}F(x)={lim}_{x\\to -{3}^{+}}-3x=-3(-3)=9\n$$\n\nand \n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to {3}^{-}}F(x)={lim}_{x\\to {3}^{-}}{x}^{2}=(3)^{2}=9.\n$$\n\nSo, ${lim}_{x\\to -{3}^{+}}F(x)={lim}_{x\\to {3}^{-}}F(x).$\n\n- Statement IV is $\\text{true}$ since statements I, II, and III are all true.\n\n**Note:** The $6$-periodic extension of $F(x)$ to $x\\in R$ has the graph shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14069003/assets/89c3a597ce1114fee9e775f291cf89e8ca04f61eb39cf2b4c896dd4be8022f09.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186359507 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "2ae32a2a-438f-547c-8510-7e9f760c3cb6" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Properties of Periodic Extensions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f36ae73e-00de-54ca-b78a-6c96b7d82c73" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "True" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359509} {:answer/id #uuid "42344ef4-478f-5b85-80b8-ce06020ee3de" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "False" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359510}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "42344ef4-478f-5b85-80b8-ce06020ee3de" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "False" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359510} :answer-field/id #uuid "c81219e4-0ddf-5b50-9940-901f22a6ced6" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359508} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d149a14b-480a-51f9-8ea6-0794ccc85a7b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "True" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359512} {:answer/id #uuid "433698e5-df60-5d8f-b2e8-3660527dceab" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "False" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359513}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d149a14b-480a-51f9-8ea6-0794ccc85a7b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "True" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359512} :answer-field/id #uuid "c4d0fd48-c014-58bb-bbcb-4c8b7d5970e3" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359511} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4a5b8564-2c8e-571f-a507-f88dd03e0c97" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "True" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359515} {:answer/id #uuid "9cf4c759-fa59-5339-bfd6-da33b55d4ba8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "False" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359516}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9cf4c759-fa59-5339-bfd6-da33b55d4ba8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "False" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359516} :answer-field/id #uuid "44c08949-d303-5df6-9ab0-e3921c78db56" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359514} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7f38b75c-9886-5bfb-bc62-878870ba47f3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "True" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359518} {:answer/id #uuid "95472977-2896-52fe-92b0-4c3e64d6178f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "False" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359519}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "95472977-2896-52fe-92b0-4c3e64d6178f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "False" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359519} :answer-field/id #uuid "7a187c9e-0e47-503e-bce4-9a2fb221d2aa" :answer-field/key "field-4" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359517}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "0295482c-764c-562f-9c52-522e737fa963" :question/math-academy-id "q-342406" :question/problem "$$\nF(x)={\\begin{aligned}x+1, & x\\in [-2,0) \\\\ -2, & x\\in [0,2)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe above function $F(x)$ is defined on $x\\in [-2,2).$ Let $f(x)$ be the $4$-periodic extension of $F(x)$ to $x\\in R.$\nSelect the correct options below.\n\n| I. | $F(x)$ is continuous on $x\\in (-2,2)$ | {{field-1}} |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| II. | $F(x)$ is piecewise smooth on $x\\in (-2,2)$ | {{field-2}} |\n| III. | ${lim}_{x\\to -{2}^{+}}F(x)={lim}_{x\\to {2}^{-}}F(x)$ | {{field-3}} |\n| IV. | $f(x)$ is piecewise smooth and continuous on $R$ | {{field-4}} |" :question/worked-solution "Let's examine the given statements in turn.\n\n- Statement I is $\\text{false}.$ The function $F(x)$ has a jump discontinuity at $x=0.$ Its graph is shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14069003/assets/7cfd6da222fb36d06be1153ac0e398e567f8b9fb8cd1cd9e21f1bb35ed131f8d.png)\n\n- Statement II is $\\text{true}.$ The function $F(x)$ is piecewise smooth on $x\\in (-2,2).$ It consists of two smooth pieces.\n\n- Statement III is $\\text{false}.$ Indeed, we have\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to -{2}^{+}}F(x)={lim}_{x\\to -{2}^{+}}(x+1)=-2+1=-1\n$$\n\nand \n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to {2}^{-}}F(x)={lim}_{x\\to {2}^{-}}(-2)=-2.\n$$\n\nSo, ${lim}_{x\\to -{2}^{+}}F(x)\\ne {lim}_{x\\to {2}^{-}}F(x).$\n\n- Statement IV is $\\text{false}$ since statements I and III are false.\n\n**Note:** The $4$-periodic extension of $F(x)$ to $x\\in R$ has the graph shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14069003/assets/a59fad69c9790a2b899c21fd730f779c28bc9b70f44a67851ad5ca92bff21951.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186359520 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "2ae32a2a-438f-547c-8510-7e9f760c3cb6" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Properties of Periodic Extensions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "cc09cee7-8414-511f-b0c9-3c63ab51a9e4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "True" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359522} {:answer/id #uuid "c753b4b8-8bc9-56ac-b594-8545bcffa664" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "False" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359523}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c753b4b8-8bc9-56ac-b594-8545bcffa664" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "False" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359523} :answer-field/id #uuid "f1b7d769-33cd-5f42-9c2b-5ed0b4dbc05e" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359521} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "23904db5-6d24-512d-94a0-9d160210e819" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "True" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359525} {:answer/id #uuid "711289ff-c36e-56ae-83cb-8ac8ceaced79" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "False" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359526}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "23904db5-6d24-512d-94a0-9d160210e819" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "True" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359525} :answer-field/id #uuid "ed844b03-a108-574b-b76f-dd35ed6e15f9" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359524} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c6990123-c3c3-54dc-b6ba-3feeecfd3e43" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "True" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359528} {:answer/id #uuid "dccd38ee-9f88-5b29-8303-fd121af1cde1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "False" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359529}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c6990123-c3c3-54dc-b6ba-3feeecfd3e43" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "True" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359528} :answer-field/id #uuid "ad66b25f-a1cb-5d37-8317-1dbb4da7426d" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359527} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0867a24f-2a09-5031-a7b3-995de8d6600e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "True" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359531} {:answer/id #uuid "f23dc740-f75d-518d-9ccc-c191ca0a438a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "False" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359532}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f23dc740-f75d-518d-9ccc-c191ca0a438a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "False" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359532} :answer-field/id #uuid "2f5d59b5-6240-541a-bf5c-68edd7004514" :answer-field/key "field-4" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359530}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "5067d48c-86e3-50e1-ac62-911ab9fb312c" :question/math-academy-id "q-342498" :question/problem "$$\nF(x)={\\begin{aligned}2x+3, & x\\in [-3,0) \\\\ (x-3)^{2}-3, & x\\in [0,3)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe above function $F(x)$ is defined on $x\\in [-3,3).$ Let $f(x)$ be the $6$-periodic extension of $F(x)$ to $x\\in R.$\nSelect the correct options below.\n\n| I. | $F(x)$ is continuous on $x\\in (-3,3)$ | {{field-1}} |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| II. | $F(x)$ is piecewise smooth on $x\\in (-3,3)$ | {{field-2}} |\n| III. | ${lim}_{x\\to -{3}^{+}}F(x)={lim}_{x\\to {3}^{-}}F(x)$ | {{field-3}} |\n| IV. | $f(x)$ is piecewise smooth and continuous on $R$ | {{field-4}} |" :question/worked-solution "Let's examine the given statements in turn.\n\n- Statement I is $\\text{false}.$ The function $F(x)$ has a jump discontinuity at $x=0.$ Its graph is shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14069003/assets/385029e7709a8d4eda45b101aba6f553c79ae3baef5b97080844e307a0b71cc7.png)\n\n- Statement II is $\\text{true}.$ The function $F(x)$ is piecewise smooth on $x\\in (-3,3).$ It consists of two smooth pieces.\n\n- Statement III is $\\text{true}.$ Indeed, we have\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to -{3}^{+}}F(x)={lim}_{x\\to -{3}^{+}}(2x+3)=2(-3)+3=-3\n$$\n\nand \n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to {3}^{-}}F(x)={lim}_{x\\to {3}^{-}}((x-3)^{2}-3)=(3-3)^{2}-3=-3.\n$$\n\nSo, ${lim}_{x\\to -{3}^{+}}F(x)={lim}_{x\\to {3}^{-}}F(x).$\n\n- Statement IV is $\\text{false}$ since statement I is false.\n\n**Note:** The $6$-periodic extension of $F(x)$ to $x\\in R$ has the graph shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14069003/assets/f4bfe80cbcc0821e93012a859ccc91b3614fa7db2df8e25399fbadc3ef7a3355.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186359533 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "2ae32a2a-438f-547c-8510-7e9f760c3cb6" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Properties of Periodic Extensions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2ce32888-42df-5b64-885e-8a1971745878" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "True" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359535} {:answer/id #uuid "88ebbf82-f896-52cc-9089-7c847462e2f4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "False" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359536}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "88ebbf82-f896-52cc-9089-7c847462e2f4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "False" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359536} :answer-field/id #uuid "660eecb1-5e21-5117-a95a-c33c899135c6" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359534} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "18eafa94-acf6-5ef0-a44f-ea107be79408" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "True" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359538} {:answer/id #uuid "9957cf99-a973-514e-8c17-6bcb9fa826f2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "False" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359539}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9957cf99-a973-514e-8c17-6bcb9fa826f2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "False" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359539} :answer-field/id #uuid "378d92f4-7cad-574e-aa0e-d621ef4c320d" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359537} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "de965145-bccc-5a63-8258-67af5011c9dc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "True" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359541} {:answer/id #uuid "6bf90920-e8dd-5702-8523-69a7f0cff152" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "False" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359542}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6bf90920-e8dd-5702-8523-69a7f0cff152" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "False" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359542} :answer-field/id #uuid "d826c523-6086-521d-b16f-8a36039323c9" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359540} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0659e5fb-ad00-5ec2-8b69-093893de172d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "True" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359544} {:answer/id #uuid "770a8cba-ea2f-530b-ad39-7d2428fa85f1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "False" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359545}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "770a8cba-ea2f-530b-ad39-7d2428fa85f1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "False" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359545} :answer-field/id #uuid "765a71d0-a1bf-52b5-a629-ea0c8eaea08c" :answer-field/key "field-4" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359543}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "24b6f004-4c8b-5565-a4ef-1d172930ca34" :question/math-academy-id "q-342657" :question/problem "$$\nF(x)={\\begin{aligned}x+2, & x\\in [-2,0] \\\\ \\frac{1}{x}, & x\\in (0,2)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe above function $F(x)$ is defined on $x\\in [-2,2).$ Let $f(x)$ be the $4$-periodic extension of $F(x)$ to $x\\in R.$\nSelect the correct options below.\n\n| I. | $F(x)$ is continuous on $x\\in (-2,2)$ | {{field-1}} |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| II. | $F(x)$ is piecewise smooth on $x\\in (-2,2)$ | {{field-2}} |\n| III. | ${lim}_{x\\to -{2}^{+}}F(x)={lim}_{x\\to {2}^{-}}F(x)$ | {{field-3}} |\n| IV. | $f(x)$ is piecewise smooth and continuous on $R$ | {{field-4}} |" :question/worked-solution "Let's examine the given statements in turn.\n\n- Statement I is $\\text{false}.$ The function $F(x)$ is not continuous on $x\\in (-2,2)$ because $\\frac{1}{x}\\to \\infty $ as $x\\to {0}^{+}.$ Its graph is shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14069003/assets/8e5eec10427a7061a05c0bd1228ce1146234bf2b09d75bb86ba83b28fbe178d9.png)\n\n- Statement II is $\\text{false}.$ The function $F(x)$ is not piecewise smooth on $x\\in (-2,2)$ because ${F}^{′}(x)=-\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}\\to -\\infty $ as $x\\to {0}^{+}.$\n\n- Statement III is $\\text{false}.$ Indeed, we have\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to -{2}^{+}}F(x)={lim}_{x\\to -{2}^{+}}(x+2)=-2+2=0\n$$\n\nand \n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to {2}^{-}}F(x)={lim}_{x\\to {2}^{-}}\\frac{1}{x}=\\frac{1}{2}.\n$$\n\nSo, ${lim}_{x\\to -{2}^{+}}F(x)\\ne {lim}_{x\\to {2}^{-}}F(x).$\n\n- Statement IV is $\\text{false}$ since statements I and II are false.\n\n**Note:** The $4$-periodic extension of $F(x)$ to $x\\in R$ has the graph shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14069003/assets/4afcdf86f777b9c7afc8af31b36cde4b80cfe394fd908db1ccd47ef48dff1617.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186359546 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "2ae32a2a-438f-547c-8510-7e9f760c3cb6" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Properties of Periodic Extensions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e6c307bb-bf83-52c3-9960-d9b58e1f1ec9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "True" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359548} {:answer/id #uuid "d7c7c192-0d6b-5503-9773-80ca89f0c6