9571} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1cd1fc39-3c79-502a-a923-5287f0be0e6d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{108(-1)^{n}}{{n}^{2}{\\pi }^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359576} {:answer/id #uuid "60b59c8c-932f-561f-a3fe-f10c4e521450" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{108(-1)^{n+1}}{{n}^{2}{\\pi }^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359577} {:answer/id #uuid "6daa124c-f89a-5425-ae91-22167fc58dd3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{36(-1)^{n+1}}{n\\pi }" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359578} {:answer/id #uuid "57361b85-0955-5174-a2e6-c88e188a15ff" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{36(-1)^{n}}{n\\pi }" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359579}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "57361b85-0955-5174-a2e6-c88e188a15ff" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{36(-1)^{n}}{n\\pi }" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359579} :answer-field/id #uuid "027e74fe-079f-57f8-a248-5ec3aa1f9e7c" :answer-field/key "field-4" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359575} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8de7aaf4-3a9a-51c2-aff3-1b09494d2d70" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{3})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359581} {:answer/id #uuid "2ee5ac9d-41e7-556a-9a28-a4e771600c4f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{3})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359582}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8de7aaf4-3a9a-51c2-aff3-1b09494d2d70" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{3})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359581} :answer-field/id #uuid "44f0ec22-25c5-56d9-b424-29c327d765c7" :answer-field/key "field-5" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359580}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "624aeef7-3c3e-595d-97ee-b38fb454f235" :question/math-academy-id "q-342963" :question/problem "Let $f(x)$ be the $6$-periodic extension of the function $F(x)=-3{x}^{2}+1$ defined on $[-3,3).$  Select the correct options in the reasoning below, showing the derivation of the Fourier series of the $6$-periodic extension of $G(x)=-6x$ from the corresponding Fourier series of $f(x).$The Fourier series of $f(x)$ is given by\n\n$$\n-3{x}^{2}+1∼-8+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{108(-1)^{n+1}}{{n}^{2}{\\pi }^{2}}{{field-1}}.\n$$\n\nSince $f$ is \n{{field-2}}\nand\n{{field-3}}\non $R,$ we may differentiate its Fourier series term-by-term to get\n\n$$\n-6x∼{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{{field-4}}\\cdot {{field-5}}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, notice that $F(x)$ is an even function. So, the Fourier series of its $2L$-periodic extension has the form\n\n$$\n\\frac{{a}_{0}}{2}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{L}).\n$$\n\nIn our case, $L=3$ and we are already given the coefficients ${a}_{0}$ and ${a}_{n}$ for $n\\ge 1.$ Thus, the Fourier series of $f(x)$ is given by\n\n$$\nf(x)∼-8+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{108(-1)^{n+1}}{{n}^{2}{\\pi }^{2}}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{3}).\n$$\n\nNow, notice that \n\n- the function $F$ is continuously differentiable on $(-3,3),$\n\n- continuous on $[-3,3),$ and\n\n- satisfies $F(-3)=F(3),$ if we extend the value at $x=3$ using the formula $F(x)=-3{x}^{2}+1.$\n\nTherefore, the $6$-periodic extension $f$ is $\\text{continuous}$ and $\\text{piecewise smooth}$ on $R,$ so we may differentiate its Fourier series term-by-term:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(-3{x}^{2}+1) & ∼\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(-8)+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{108(-1)^{n+1}}{{n}^{2}{\\pi }^{2}}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{3})) \\\\ -6x & ∼0+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{108(-1)^{n+1}}{{n}^{2}{\\pi }^{2}}\\cdot (-\\frac{n\\pi }{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{3})) \\\\ -6x & ∼{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{-36(-1)^{n+1}}{n\\pi }\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{3}) \\\\ -6x & ∼{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\,\\frac{36(-1)^{n}}{n\\pi }\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{3})\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186359583 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f2e37d37-007c-569b-a44c-cb6a9d075371" :knowledge-point/title "Differentiating a Fourier Series"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b1a51910-98dd-5069-bd0a-a4b5ea29be94" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{10})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359585} {:answer/id #uuid "04772204-de26-5cc7-aeea-30b79b998f2a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{5})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359586} {:answer/id #uuid "93e81119-231c-5c83-af9c-cda532afca58" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{10})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359587} {:answer/id #uuid "a211c4ae-7055-53dc-b72e-c3a975af5a2a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{5})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359588}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "04772204-de26-5cc7-aeea-30b79b998f2a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{5})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359586} :answer-field/id #uuid "b392473d-00e9-5e13-852e-56e9556bdb04" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359584} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1b004c35-03c7-545a-b3af-aee3a1b1d069" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "even" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359590} {:answer/id #uuid "d57455e0-d6e1-5c6f-bea7-122049dcad84" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "odd" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186