 "0af2ac91-651e-5dc6-9c91-cd2ec7a482ca" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{15(-1)^{n}}{n\\pi }" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359601}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0af2ac91-651e-5dc6-9c91-cd2ec7a482ca" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{15(-1)^{n}}{n\\pi }" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359601} :answer-field/id #uuid "c7557fe4-ab09-56b2-85d8-21a8958a39f9" :answer-field/key "field-4" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359597} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "69393008-162b-5dd7-8b7c-a7760a9d0a2e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{5})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359603} {:answer/id #uuid "64efde4c-3bc0-5f59-a8be-ccc48d6d9c10" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{5})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359604}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "64efde4c-3bc0-5f59-a8be-ccc48d6d9c10" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{5})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359604} :answer-field/id #uuid "a04cbf9a-d9d8-5bb8-8c52-1c5722c4e578" :answer-field/key "field-5" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359602}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "7379723f-56d8-5cec-a825-183cb7d85e67" :question/math-academy-id "q-343247" :question/problem "Let $f(x)$ be the $10$-periodic extension of the function $F(x)=-\\frac{3}{4}{x}^{2}+5$ defined on $[-5,5).$ Select the correct options in the reasoning below, showing the derivation of the Fourier series of the $10$-periodic extension of $G(x)=-\\frac{3}{2}x$ from the corresponding Fourier series of $f(x).$The Fourier series of $f(x)$ is given by\n\n$$\n-\\frac{3}{4}{x}^{2}+5∼-\\frac{5}{4}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{75(-1)^{n+1}}{{n}^{2}{\\pi }^{2}}{{field-1}}.\n$$\n\nSince $f$ is \n{{field-2}}\nand\n{{field-3}}\non $R,$ we may differentiate its Fourier series term-by-term to get\n\n$$\n-\\frac{3}{2}x∼{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{{field-4}}\\cdot {{field-5}}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, notice that $F(x)$ is an even function. So, the Fourier series of its $2L$-periodic extension has the form\n\n$$\n\\frac{{a}_{0}}{2}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{L}).\n$$\n\nIn our case, $L=5$ and we are already given the coefficients ${a}_{0}$ and ${a}_{n}$ for $n\\ge 1.$ Thus, the Fourier series of $f(x)$ is given by\n\n$$\nf(x)∼-\\frac{5}{4}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{75(-1)^{n+1}}{{n}^{2}{\\pi }^{2}}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{5}).\n$$\n\nNow, notice that \n\n- the function $F$ is continuously differentiable on $(-5,5),$\n\n- continuous on $[-5,5),$ and\n\n- satisfies $F(-5)=F(5),$ if we extend the value at $x=5$ using the formula $F(x)=-\\frac{3}{4}{x}^{2}+5.$\n\nTherefore, the $10$-periodic extension $f$ is $\\text{continuous}$ and $\\text{piecewise smooth}$ on $R,$ so we may differentiate its Fourier series term-by-term:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(-\\frac{3}{4}{x}^{2}+5) & ∼\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(-\\frac{5}{4})+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{75(-1)^{n+1}}{{n}^{2}{\\pi }^{2}}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{5})) \\\\ -\\frac{3}{2}x & ∼0+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{75(-1)^{n+1}}{{n}^{2}{\\pi }^{2}}\\cdot (-\\frac{n\\pi }{5}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{5})) \\\\ -\\frac{3}{2}x & ∼{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{-15(-1)^{n+1}}{n\\pi }\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{5}) \\\\ -\\frac{3}{2}x & ∼{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\,\\frac{15(-1)^{n}}{n\\pi }\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{5})\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186359605 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c1e01d04-6c13-52eb-a4b6-ad9a5cde8134" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating a Fourier Series"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "fb737a03-be23-507d-8141-d45cfe133efc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{cos}⁡(n\\pi x)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359607} {:answer/id #uuid "1b31ec0a-59d7-5822-a5b0-c95f3a4b74b2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{sin}⁡(nx)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359608} {:answer/id #uuid "1752a6cb-7b0c-574e-b643-5d3e72accff8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{cos}⁡(nx)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359609} {:answer/id #uuid "a3d3e58b-4ce2-5f5b-bd59-bc239591ed7d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{2})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359610} {:answer/id #uuid "939c4497-1c10-5918-abca-288df4b1596a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{2})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359611} {:answer/id #uuid "c48d1f4d-da82-5992-acad-8307d21885bb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{sin}⁡(n\\pi x)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359612}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c48d1f4d-da82-5992-acad-8307d21885bb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{sin}⁡(n\\pi x)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359612} :answer-field/id #uuid "d49a3228-7799-5e35-82bd-cd323fb6d807" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359606} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8e53ddcb-6002-5a9e-b7a9-60dbf9159c1e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "even" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359614} {:answer/id #uuid "b9dc4c72-bcce-52dc-a464-5e786e66d11a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "periodic" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359615} {:answer/id #uuid "0dd32099-6994-55a4-8e86-9e0f1daef9f4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "piecewise continuous" :db/id #edb/ref