db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{5}))" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359667} :answer-field/id #uuid "c84db665-a52b-55d4-bb57-bb3076f2ce3c" :answer-field/key "field-4" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359665}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "de25ec60-135e-5b0f-93ec-2a89a92381de" :question/math-academy-id "q-343341" :question/problem "Let $f(x)$ be the $10$-periodic extension of the function $F(x)=5x$ defined on $[-5,5).$ Select the correct options in the reasoning below, showing the derivation of a series converging to the $10$-periodic extension of \n\n$$\nG(x)=\\frac{5}{2}{x}^{2}={\\int }_{0}^{x}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t\n$$\n\nfrom the corresponding Fourier series of $f(x).$The Fourier series of $f(x)$ is given by\n\n$$\n5x∼{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{50(-1)^{n+1}}{n\\pi }{{field-1}}.\n$$\n\nSince $f$ is \n{{field-2}} \non $R,$ we may integrate its Fourier series term-by-term to get\n\n$$\n\\frac{5}{2}{x}^{2}∼{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{{field-3}}\\cdot {{field-4}}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, notice that $F(x)$ is an odd function. So, the Fourier series of its $2L$-periodic extension has the form\n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{b}_{n}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{L}).\n$$\n\nIn our case, $L=5$ and we are already given the coefficients ${b}_{n}$ for $n\\ge 1.$ Thus, the Fourier series of $f(x)$ is given by\n\n$$\nf(x)∼{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{50(-1)^{n+1}}{n\\pi }\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{5}).\n$$\n\nNow, notice that the function $F$ is continuous on $(-5,5).$ \nTherefore, the $10$-periodic extension $f$ is $\\text{piecewise continuous}$ on $R,$ so we may integrate its Fourier series term-by-term:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{x}5t\\,\\text{d}t & ∼{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{\\int }_{0}^{x}\\frac{50(-1)^{n+1}}{n\\pi }\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi t}{5})\\,\\text{d}t \\\\ {[\\frac{5}{2}{t}^{2}]}_{0}^{x} & ∼{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{50(-1)^{n+1}}{n\\pi }\\cdot [-\\frac{5}{n\\pi }\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi t}{5})]_{0}^{x} \\\\ \\frac{5}{2}{x}^{2} & ∼{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\,\\frac{250(-1)^{n+1}}{{n}^{2}{\\pi }^{2}}\\cdot (1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{5}))\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186221974 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c1e01d04-6c13-52eb-a4b6-ad9a5cde8134" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating a Fourier Series"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a9866a9a-cead-5ab4-bdea-07cb41581b32" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sin ((nπx)/(2))" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186220836} {:answer/id #uuid "d62fee15-3bf9-57c0-8128-f008610aa956" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\cos ((nπx)/(4))" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186220837} {:answer/id #uuid "15997c6c-66a6-59c4-b68b-94125650f15d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\cos ((nπx)/(2))" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186220838} {:answer/id #uuid "6886af66-8dde-5442-8b37-70cae88d2d94" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sin ((nπx)/(4))" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186220839}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "15997c6c-66a6-59c4-b68b-94125650f15d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\cos ((nπx)/(2))" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186220838} :answer-field/id #uuid "d744c883-6921-5db7-8067-f37aa8ebe190" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186220835} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "dce6e597-e3f8-5d4a-8ce8-e79f692769de" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "even" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359671} {:answer/id #uuid "159576c2-a6eb-59b0-ac55-b7c67187618f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "periodic" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359672} {:answer/id #uuid "0661e56c-183e-5dfe-8a8b-5098fb468d